        "knowledge_point": "Solving a \"Greater Than or Equal To\" Inequality Given the Graph of the Corresponding Parabola",
        "problem": "![](images/09/098189dc8e96b01cb045a198eef3f00ba2df6594fc14675cad81246fc2d25964.png)\n\nGiven the graph above, solve the inequality $(x+2)(x-3)\\ge 0.$",
        "worked_solution": "Notice that our inequality\n\n$$\n(x+2)(x-3)\\ge 0\n$$\n\nis a \"*greater than or equal to*\" inequality. Therefore, we need to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola \n\n$$\ny=(x+2)(x-3)\n$$\n\nis *above* the $x$-axis or *touches* this axis. We mark these values of $x$ in blue in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/3e/3e80a6e08ccff87314e5081a08332f0de508f6db02446742d1c93416d41a4b3c.png)\n\nSo, the solution to the inequality is $x\\le -2$ or $x\\ge 3.$",
